UPDATE companies SET description='Circuit Tech Assembly, LLC operates from West Berlin in Berlin Township, New Jersey. The company was founded in 2004 by the Sherlock family, with Bill Sherlock Jr. serving as president and Bill Sherlock Sr. handling business development. It began as a contract electronic manufacturing and design firm focused on exceeding customer procurement goals through a process-driven philosophy.

The shop provides a full range of electronic manufacturing services: PCB fabrication, surface-mount and plated through-hole assembly, wire and cable assembly, electro-mechanical assembly, and box build. Engineering support includes design and test engineering using PADS software, along with quality and material management. The company handles prototypes, pilot runs, and full production volumes.

Primary markets served are the transit industry (rolling stock), telecommunications, and defense/military sectors. Customers in these industries rely on the firm for both printed circuit board fabrication and higher-level electro-mechanical integration.

The company emphasizes an unwavering philosophy of automation and a process model that builds quality into the product. Its stated aim is to deliver priced product that exceeds customer expectations through automated, repeatable processes.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Fabrication", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT)", "Plated Through Hole Assembly", "Wire and Cable Assembly", "Electro-Mechanical Assembly", "Box Build", "Design Engineering (PADS)", "Test Engineering", "Quality Management", "Material Management"], "industries": ["Transit / Rolling Stock", "Telecommunications", "Defense / Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["PADS design software"], "volume": "Prototype to production volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Process model with quality built in", "Automation-focused manufacturing philosophy", "Prototype through production volume range", "PADS for engineering design changes and initial design"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2004 -> db", "Location West Berlin, NJ -> page /", "Family ownership (Bill Sherlock Jr./Sr.) -> page /", "Contract electronic manufacturing & design -> page /", "Services list (PCB fab, SMT, PTH, wire/cable, electro-mech, box build, design, test, quality, material mgmt) -> page /", "Industries: Transit, Telecom, Defense -> industries_served db", "ISO 9001 certification -> certifications db", "PADS for design -> capabilities db", "Prototypes, Pilots and Productions -> products db", "Automation philosophy and process model -> products db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Electronic Manufacturing & Design", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='circuit-tech-assembly' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cirtec Medical is headquartered in Brooklyn Park, Minnesota. The company operates as a contract development and manufacturing partner for Class II and III medical technologies, though its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides integrated services spanning precision extrusion, braiding, coiling, and laser processing for catheter systems; micron-level CNC machining and Swiss milling for metal components; thin-film deposition, custom ASIC design, and flexible electronics for implantable and wearable devices; and silicone and synthetic polyisoprene molding for drug-delivery and tubing applications. It also offers balloon forming, electrode integration, and high-speed stamping for high-volume production of intricate metal parts.

Cirtec serves medical device OEMs targeting neurovascular, structural heart, electrophysiology, cardiovascular, and interventional markets. Its customer base includes medical device companies that rely on the firm for concept-through-commercialization support on complex Class II and III programs.

The company emphasizes three differentiators: accelerated time to market through flexible, integrated design and development; a quality management system validated for Class III devices that can integrate with client systems; and reduced risk by consolidating design, engineering, and manufacturing under one roof to eliminate handoff delays.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision extrusion", "Braiding", "Coiling", "Delivery sheath systems", "Laser processing", "Micron-level CNC machining", "Swiss milling", "High-speed stamping", "High-precision laser welding, cutting, and marking", "Thin-film technology", "Custom ASIC design", "Flexible electronics fabrication", "Balloon forming", "Electrode integration", "Silicone molding", "Synthetic polyisoprene processing", "Medical tubing extrusion", "Drug delivery system manufacturing", "Printed circuit board assembly", "Precision metal component fabrication", "Catheter subassembly manufacturing"], "industries": ["Neurovascular", "Structural heart", "Electrophysiology", "Cardiovascular", "Implantable medical devices", "Wearable medical devices", "Drug delivery systems", "Interventional devices"], "materials": ["Silicone", "Synthetic polyisoprene", "Biocompatible metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Micron-level precision", "built_on": ["Accelerated time to market via integrated design, development, and manufacturing", "Quality management system validated for Class III devices", "Reduced risk by eliminating multi-partner handoffs", "Three decades of microelectronics and thin-film expertise", "Configurable catheter handle platform (Navigator) and neurostimulation platform (ACCEL+)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brooklyn Park, Minnesota -> db", "Specializes in advanced catheter technologies: precision extrusion, braiding, coiling, delivery sheath systems, laser processing -> db", "Offers micron-level CNC machining, Swiss milling, laser processing for Class II/III devices -> /", "Provides thin-film technology, custom ASICs, flexible electronics for implantable/wearable systems -> /", "Supplies silicone and synthetic polyisoprene for implantable devices, drug delivery, medical tubing -> /", "Serves neurovascular, structural heart, electrophysiology, cardiovascular markets -> db, /", "Differentiators: accelerated time to market, quality management system for Class III, reduced risk via integration -> /", "Three decades of microelectronics expertise -> /", "Platforms: ACCEL+ Neurostimulation Platform, Navigator Catheter Handle Platform -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Your partner from concept to commercialization, rapidly developing and scaling Class II and III medical technologies.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cirtec-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Sofa of NY traces its roots to 1982, when it began as a Brooklyn-based factory crafting benchmade furniture. The company later relocated its production to a facility at 728 East 136th Street in the Bronx, New York, while maintaining showrooms in Manhattan, Palm Beach, and Nantucket. In 2012, Blake Anding assumed ownership as President and Head of Design, steering the brand toward a vertically integrated model that keeps design and manufacturing under one roof.

The firm produces custom upholstered furniture, drapery, and large-scale furnishings using old-world, hand-crafted techniques. Its Bronx factory turns out benchmade frames from locally sourced hardwoods, and the team offers in-home consultations, progress sit-tests, on-site build, installation, and white-glove delivery. Specialty projects extend to custom wall coverings, window treatments, and full interior outfitting for hospitality venues, yachts, and private jets.

Clients span custom residential, trade (interior designers and architects), and commercial sectors. Concrete examples include hospitality installations, yacht interiors, and private-jet cabin furnishings.

The company differentiates itself with a lifetime frame guarantee, a commitment to sustainability through longevity, and a Savile Row–level attention to detail that stems from Anding’s English heritage. The vertical operation ensures consistency from design through final inspection.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom upholstered furniture", "Custom drapery", "Benchmade furniture construction", "In-home consultations and measurements", "Progress sit-tests", "On-site build and installation", "White-glove delivery", "Large-scale upholstered furnishings", "Custom wall coverings", "Window treatments", "Full-service interior outfitting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Trade (interior design/architecture)", "Commercial", "Hospitality", "Marine (yachts)", "Aviation (private jets)"], "materials": ["Hardwood (locally sourced)", "Eco-friendly raw materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime guarantee on frames", "Benchmade, bespoke furniture handcrafted in NYC since 1982", "Vertical integration: design and production in-house at Bronx factory", "In-home consultations, progress sit-tests, on-site build, installation, white-glove delivery", "Specialty projects for hospitality, yachts, and private jets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 in Brooklyn -> /about", "Bronx factory location -> /about and /", "Blake Anding took ownership in 2012 -> /about", "Frames guaranteed for life -> /about and /", "In-home consultations, progress sit-tests, on-site build, installation, white-glove delivery -> /", "Specialty projects for hospitality, yachts, private jets -> /", "Vertical operation design and production in-house -> /about", "Showrooms in Manhattan, Palm Beach, Nantucket -> / and /about", "Locally-sourced hardwood frames -> /about", "Eco-friendly raw materials -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "benchmade, bespoke furniture expertly handcrafted in New York City since 1982", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='classic-sofa-of-ny' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clear-Vu Lighting operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in Central Islip, New York. The company traces its roots to 1957 when LaMar Lighting was founded in Garden City South, NY. The Clear-Vu brand was launched in 2008 by Autronic Plastics, which acquired LaMar Lighting in 2020, uniting the two legacies under single ownership. Founder and CEO Daniel Lax leads the business, which emphasizes union-made, American manufacturing.

The firm designs and produces LED lighting systems for six specialized markets: transit, construction, commercial and industrial, healthcare, life sciences, and correctional facilities. Manufacturing is vertically integrated, encompassing in-house plastic injection molding, CNC tooling, LED assembly, optical testing, and a dedicated R&D lab. The facility runs 78-plus product lines and has installed more than 500,000 Occu-Smart motion-sensor units.

Customers include transit agencies such as the MTA — for which Clear-Vu supplied over 20 custom fixtures across 15 New York City subway stations — as well as federal agencies, commercial builders, healthcare institutions, and life-sciences manufacturers. The company also serves correctional facilities with vandal-resistant, ligature-resistant fixtures.

Clear-Vu differentiates itself through full vertical integration, BABA/BAA compliance, and a no-outsourcing policy that keeps design, prototyping, and production under one roof. The company states its mission is to deliver purpose-built, engineered lighting systems for demanding environments rather than generic fixtures.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Listed','DLC Listed','BABA/BAA Compliant','LEED','NSF P442','Union Made']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["In-house plastic injection molding", "In-house CNC tooling and mold making", "LED assembly and testing", "Optical testing", "Custom fixture design and prototyping", "Wireless monitoring (clearNET)", "DALI emergency backup systems", "Low-voltage temporary site lighting", "Motion-sensor lighting (Occu-Smart)", "Surgical illumination systems", "Cleanroom-rated LED fixtures (ISO3-ISO8)", "Vandal-resistant and tamper-proof fixtures", "Ligature-resistant fixtures", "Architectural and linear LED lighting", "Sensor-controlled LED systems"], "industries": ["Transit", "Construction", "Commercial & Industrial", "Healthcare", "Life Sciences", "Correctional & Secure"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses", "CNC tooling equipment", "LED assembly lines", "Optical testing stations", "R&D lab"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing with in-house injection molding, tooling, and LED assembly", "BABA/BAA compliant and union-made using American labor", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Direct engineering support from the design team", "69 years of lighting innovation including first LED-lit subway tunnel"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1957 as LaMar Lighting -> /about-us", "Clear-Vu brand launched 2008 by Autronic Plastics -> /about-us", "Autronic Plastics acquired LaMar Lighting 2020 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Central Islip, NY -> /about-us", "100,000 sq ft vertically integrated facility -> /about-us", "In-house plastic injection molding, tooling, LED assembly -> /about-us", "78+ product lines -> /about-us", "6 specialized markets (transit, construction, commercial/industrial, healthcare, life sciences, correctional) -> /about-us", "500,000+ Occu-Smart units installed -> /", "NYC Subway Enhanced Station Initiative: 20+ custom fixtures across 15 stations -> /", "BABA/BAA compliant, union made, ISO 9001:2015 -> /", "DLC Listed options -> /", "NSF P442 First Certification -> /about-us", "LEED Innovation in Design award -> /about-us", "Founder & CEO Daniel Lax -> /about-us", "130+ years combined engineering experience -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Engineered, manufactured, and supported from our Long Island, New York facility.", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clear-vu-lighting' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clearloop Corporation is based in Nashville, Tennessee. The company was founded as a carbon solution by three Tennesseans — Bob Corney, Laura Zapata, and Gov. Phil Bredesen — who wanted the environmental, health, and economic benefits of clean energy to reach communities that need them most, starting in their own region. Clearloop was later acquired by Silicon Ranch, one of the largest independent power producers in the United States, to deliver on that promise at scale.

The company develops carbon solutions that help organizations measure their emissions, reclaim them by building new solar capacity in the most carbon-intense parts of the U.S. electricity grid, and track the resulting clean energy generation. Rather than purchasing power from existing projects, Clearloop finances and facilitates the development of new solar installations in locations such as Arcadia, Louisiana; Jackson, Tennessee; Panola County, Mississippi; Paris, Tennessee; and White Pine, Tennessee. Their model charges partners a fee based on a percentage of the product or corporate carbon footprint, directing those funds into new solar construction.

Clearloop works with companies of all sizes, from global corporations to small businesses and educational institutions, that want to offset their carbon footprint and expand access to clean energy. Partners receive a "100% reclaimed carbon footprint®" certification for products or services tied to the investment. The firm focuses on the U.S. South, where grid carbon intensity is highest, arguing that building solar there displaces more fossil-fuel generation per watt than in cleaner regions.

The founders started Clearloop as outsiders to corporate sustainability with a pragmatic, optimistic approach to climate action. They aim to green the U.S. electricity grid by 2050 by turning everyday purchases and corporate commitments into new renewable energy projects that benefit underserved communities. The company emphasizes equal access, low-risk long-term investment, corporate accountability, and scalable commitment as core principles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Carbon footprint measurement", "Solar project development and financing", "Carbon offset verification and tracking", "Corporate sustainability consulting", "Renewable energy project siting in high-impact regions"], "industries": ["Corporate sustainability", "Renewable energy development", "Carbon offset markets", "Educational institutions", "Global corporations", "Small businesses"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Builds new solar projects rather than buying from existing ones", "Focuses on carbon-intense grid regions in the U.S. South", "Offers \"100% reclaimed carbon footprint\u00ae\" certification for partners", "Scales from product-level to company-wide carbon reclamation", "Fee based on percentage of product or corporate carbon footprint"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nashville, Tennessee -> db", "Founded by three Tennesseans: Bob Corney, Laura Zapata, Gov. Phil Bredesen -> /about", "Acquired by Silicon Ranch -> /about", "Business model: measure emissions, reclaim by building new solar, track progress -> /", "Projects in Arcadia LA, Jackson TN, Panola County MS, Paris TN, White Pine TN -> /", "Serves global corporations, small businesses, educational institutions -> /about", "\"100% reclaimed carbon footprint\u00ae\" trademark -> /about", "Fee based on percentage of product/corporate carbon footprint -> /about", "Focus on U.S. South carbon-intense grid regions -> /about", "Goal to green U.S. grid by 2050 -> /about", "Team members listed (Jaclyn Mothupi, Emily Fairbank, etc.) -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Clearloop creates carbon solutions for organizations of all sizes... to decarbonize the economy, expand access to clean energy, and accelerate the development of new solar projects", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/clearloop-corporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clearloop-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Click Bond, Inc. is headquartered in Carson City, Nevada. The company specializes in adhesive-bonded fasteners and does not disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founders in the provided materials.

The company designs and manufactures a range of adhesive-bonded fastening products including ACRES® sleeves, rivetless nutplates, bushings, mounts, studs and standoffs, and adhesives. It also offers custom engineering services to develop tailored fastening solutions. The product portfolio includes hundreds of iterative designs not listed in the public catalog.

Click Bond serves aerospace, defense, marine, automotive, rail, energy, and industrial sectors. Specific markets include commercial, military, and general aviation; business jets; advanced air mobility; rotorcraft; unmanned systems; satellites; missiles; engines; offshore and naval vessels; military vehicles; heavy trucks; automotive and rail transit; and green energy. Applications span cable and wiring management, fuel and fluid tanks, interiors, pressurized vessels, decking, equipment attachment, tubing, repairs, panels, and systems attachment.

The company emphasizes its engineering team''s ability to pioneer advanced fastening solutions for challenging designs and highlights a global network of local representatives to support customers worldwide.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Adhesive-bonded fastener manufacturing", "Custom fastener design and engineering", "ACRES\u00ae sleeve production", "Rivetless nutplate production", "Bushing and mount fabrication", "Stud and standoff manufacturing", "Adhesive formulation and supply"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Marine", "Automotive", "Rail", "Energy", "Industrial", "Commercial Aviation", "Military Aviation", "General Aviation", "Business Jets", "Advanced Air Mobility", "Rotorcraft", "Unmanned Systems", "Satellites", "Missiles", "Engines", "Offshore", "Naval", "Military Vehicles", "Heavy Trucks", "Rail Transit", "Green Energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hundreds of iterative products not shown in online database", "Customized designs engineered for specific applications", "Global network of local representatives"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Carson City, Nevada -> db", "Product: Adhesive-bonded fasteners -> page /", "Product lines: ACRES\u00ae Sleeves, Rivetless Nutplates, Bushings, Mounts, Studs & Standoffs, Adhesives -> page /", "Custom solutions offered -> page /", "Markets: Aerospace, Defense, Marine, Automotive, Rail, Energy, Industrial -> page /", "Specific industries listed (aviation, space, marine, land, industrial) -> page /", "Applications: Cables & Wiring, Fuel & Fluid Tanks, Interiors, Pressurized Vessels, etc. -> page /", "Global rep network mentioned -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Click Bond, Inc. - Adhesive-Bonded Fasteners For Aerospace, Defense, Marine, Automotive, Rail, Energy, & Industrial Sectors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "",