UPDATE companies SET description='Club Ride Apparel is based in Hailey, Idaho, and was founded in the spring of 2008 by Mike Herlinger. Herlinger, then working at an outdoor store and racing mountain bikes on weekends, conceived the brand after a ride in Sun Valley when he wondered why he couldn''t ride in his favorite vintage Western shirt. That moment sparked a line of clothing that blends technical cycling performance with Western-inspired style.

The company designs and sells mountain lifestyle apparel for men and women, including long- and short-sleeve shirts, jackets, pants, shorts, chamois, gloves, and socks. Club Ride also offers a custom apparel program for teams and shops. The brand operates primarily through its e-commerce site and a network of retail partners.

Club Ride serves the outdoor recreation market, targeting mountain bikers, hikers, raft guides, ski bums, and self-described weekend warriors who split time between work and backcountry pursuits. Its gear is designed for riders who want performance on the trail without sacrificing style off the bike.

Herlinger''s original conviction—that cycling kit can be both technical and stylish—remains the company''s differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom apparel production", "Apparel design and development", "Technical fabric sourcing"], "industries": ["Cycling", "Mountain biking", "Outdoor recreation", "Adventure sports", "Sportswear"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founder Mike Herlinger, founded spring 2008 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Hailey, Idaho -> db", "Product categories: tops, bottoms, chamois, jackets, gloves, socks -> /", "Custom apparel program -> /", "Differentiators: Rider-owned, Designed durable, Bike forward details -> /", "Company makes apparel -> /about-us", "Industries served: mountain bikers, hikers, raft guides, ski bums -> /about-us", "Free shipping on US orders over $125 -> /", "Irreverent style, technical fabrics, mountain vibes -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We make apparel for riders who live their lives on two wheels and never take themselves too seriously on the bike or off.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='club-ride-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='REC''s sister company, Nexus Line, LLC, simultaneously purchased the high-voltage direct current (HVDC) transmission line that carries power from the station to the Dickinson converter station near Buffalo, Minnesota.

REC describes its portfolio as spanning generation, transmission, wind, and carbon capture, aiming to harness natural resources for a sustainable future.

The company emphasizes local procurement, citing Captain''s Cabin, a vendor in the Underwood area, as an example of its commitment to keeping business within the community. REC states that its wages and spending help fuel the local economy.

REC positions itself as a provider of reliable, affordable, and increasingly clean energy. Its stated mission centers on safety, environmental consciousness, and improving the lives of community members through integrity and accountability. The company highlights the plant''s efficiency and its investments in carbon capture as differentiators in the transition to cleaner energy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power generation", "Electricity transmission", "Wind energy development", "Carbon capture"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Coal Creek Station", "HVDC transmission line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["North Dakota''s most efficient power plant", "Reliable, affordable, and increasingly clean energy", "Commitment to keeping business local and supporting small communities", "HVDC transmission line ownership via sister company Nexus Line"], "facts_used": ["Rainbow Energy Center, LLC owns Coal Creek Station -> /about", "Acquired May 1, 2022 -> /about", "Approximately 200 employees -> /about", "Nexus Line, LLC owns HVDC transmission line -> /", "Generation, Transmission, Wind, Carbon Capture activities -> /about", "Commitment to reliable, affordable, increasingly clean energy -> /", "Local vendor example: Captain''s Cabin -> /about", "Headquarters in Underwood, North Dakota -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Rainbow Energy Center, LLC (REC) is the proud owner of North Dakota''s most efficient power plant, Coal Creek Station", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "approximately 200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='coal-creek-station' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Coastal Power Systems operates from Tomball, Texas, in the Houston metropolitan area. The company was founded in 1995 as a supplier of industrial circuit breakers and has since expanded into a full-service provider of electrical power distribution solutions.

The firm manufactures custom power distribution equipment including UL 1558 switchgear, UL 891 switchboards, UL 67 panelboards, and medium- and low-voltage switchgear, along with protection and control systems. Its capabilities span engineering and design studies (coordination, arc flash, short circuit), NETA-guided testing and commissioning, preventive maintenance, circuit breaker restoration, switchgear modernization, arc flash mitigation, and 24/7 emergency response. Field services cover primary and secondary injection testing, protective relay testing, equipment repair, and refurbishment. The company also supplies new, reconditioned, and obsolete industrial circuit breakers with retrofit kits and parts.

Coastal Power Systems serves utilities, data centers, power generation facilities, oil and gas operations, petrochemical plants, industrial manufacturers, water and wastewater systems, transportation infrastructure, commercial buildings, and renewable energy sites. Its customers include EPC firms, consulting engineers, and mission-critical operators who require single-source responsibility for electrical infrastructure from design through lifecycle support.

The company emphasizes an integrated model that combines engineering, manufacturing, field service, testing, repair, and modernization under one roof. Its stated mission is to deliver dependable, responsive, and practical power solutions that improve reliability, reduce downtime, and support long-term performance of critical electrical infrastructure. The tagline "We Build What We Sell. We Support What We Build." reflects this end-to-end approach.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 1558','UL 891','UL 67','NETA-guided testing procedures']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering and design services", "Power system coordination studies", "Arc flash studies", "Short circuit studies", "Reliability assessments", "Manufacturing of UL 1558 switchgear", "Manufacturing of UL 891 switchboards", "Manufacturing of UL 67 panelboards", "Medium voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Low voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Protection and control systems manufacturing", "NETA-guided testing and commissioning", "Primary injection testing", "Secondary injection testing", "Protective relay testing", "Electrical preventive maintenance", "Circuit breaker inspection, maintenance, and repair", "Full circuit breaker restoration and reconditioning", "Infrared thermography inspections", "Switchgear and switchboard maintenance", "Motor control center maintenance, repair, and refurbishment", "Circuit breaker retrofits and retrofills", "Switchgear modernization", "Arc flash mitigation", "Obsolete equipment programs", "24/7 emergency response", "Emergency equipment replacement", "Field services for commissioning, testing, maintenance, repair, and refurbishment", "Industrial circuit breaker sales, repairs, retrofits, and parts"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Data centers", "Power generation", "Oil and gas", "Petrochemical", "Industrial manufacturing", "Water and wastewater", "Transportation infrastructure", "Commercial facilities", "Renewables", "Mission-critical environments", "EPC firms", "Consulting engineers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house manufacturing with engineering-first approach", "NETA-guided testing procedures", "Field service and manufacturing support under one roof", "24/7 emergency support for urgent power system issues", "Single point of responsibility with faster communication"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 -> /about", "Headquarters Tomball, Texas -> /", "Manufactures UL 1558 switchgear, UL 891 switchboards, UL 67 panelboards -> /", "NETA-guided testing -> /", "Industries served: utilities, data centers, power generation, oil and gas, petrochemical, industrial, water/wastewater, transportation, commercial, renewables -> /", "Integrated engineering, manufacturing, field services, testing, maintenance, modernization, emergency response -> /", "24/7 emergency support -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Coastal Power Systems manufactures and supports custom power distribution equipment for industrial, utility, commercial, and mission-critical applications.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/coastal-power-systems/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='coastal-power-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cola Foods has operated from Cranston, Rhode Island since 1958. The family-owned business began as a small facility and has grown over six decades while remaining under the stewardship of the Colagiovanni family, with John Colagiovanni serving as president and his son Gio as vice president, supported by general manager Kevin Fellela and controller Giana D''Ercole.

The company manufactures a range of specialty meat products under its own brands—Giovanni''s, Lincoln Brand, and Marcello—including sausages made from time-honored recipes, shaved steak and other shaved meats, artisanal specialty cuts, and ground beef, chicken, and pork.

Its private-label program allows retailers and foodservice operators to bring their own branded meat products to market, while its branded lines are available through a store locator that points consumers to nearby retail locations.

