UPDATE companies SET description='Commercial Radio Company, Inc. operates from Cavendish, Vermont, where it was founded in 1970 by engineer Dan Churchill. Churchill, known for his hands-on troubleshooting on transmitting towers, built the business around distributing Cornell-Dubilier mica capacitors. Today the company remains a second-generation family enterprise focused on supplying mica capacitors for emerging semiconductor applications.

The firm acts as a stocking distributor for the full Cornell-Dubilier mica capacitor line, including Types 271, 272, 273, 291, 292, 293, 294, and the HT, HK, AT, and AK series. Its inventory spans thousands of part numbers — such as NL523W02-004, NL523W03-010, and 29280B242JO0 — all held in stock for immediate shipment. The company emphasizes rapid fulfillment, with a team available across multiple time zones to accelerate order processing.

Customers span aerospace and defense, medical equipment, counter-drone systems, electronic warfare, wind and solar power, electric-vehicle charging infrastructure, military programs, and broadcast radio stations. The capacitors are specified in high-frequency RF designs where stable capacitance and minimal drift are critical.

Commercial Radio Company differentiates itself by maintaining what it describes as the largest U.S. inventory of Cornell-Dubilier mica capacitors, offering competitive pricing backed by a price-match guarantee, and supplying U.S.-made components that avoid tariffs. The founder’s original commitment to hands-on technical support continues through a round-the-clock service model.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Stocking distribution of Cornell-Dubilier mica capacitors", "Technical support for capacitor selection and troubleshooting", "Rapid order fulfillment and shipping", "Inventory management for high-frequency RF components"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "Medical Equipment", "Counter Drone Technology", "Electronic Warfare", "Wind Energy", "Solar Energy", "Electric Vehicle Charging", "Military Applications", "Broadcast Radio"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest U.S. inventory of Cornell-Dubilier mica capacitors", "Competitive pricing with price-match guarantee (free T-shirt if beaten)", "U.S.-manufactured components, no tariffs", "Round-the-clock technical support across time zones", "Second-generation family ownership"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1970 by Dan Churchill -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Cavendish, Vermont -> db", "World''s largest stocking distributor for Cornell-Dubilier (CDM) capacitors -> /about-us", "Carries largest inventory of Mica Capacitors in the United States -> /about-us", "Second-generation family business -> /about-us", "Supplies mica capacitor types 271, 272, 273, 291, 292, 293, 294, HT, HK, AT, AK -> /about-us", "Serves aerospace and defense, medical equipment, counter drone, electronic warfare, wind, solar, EV charging, military, broadcast radio -> /about-us, db", "Specific part numbers: NL523W02-004, NL523W03-010, NL523W04-020, 27250B470JO0, NL523W03-024, AK25B103JN, 29280B242JO0 -> /, /about-us", "Competitive pricing with