UPDATE companies SET description='Complete Cable Company LLC is a family-owned manufacturer of custom wire harnesses and cable assemblies based in St. Joseph, Michigan. The company is led by co-owners Rob Kasun and Jon Kasun, who oversee business operations, production, and quality execution.

The company produces wire harnesses and cable assemblies from prototype through repeat production, handling wire cutting, stripping, crimping, and assembly for gauges ranging from 14 to 22 AWG with PVC and SRPVC insulation. Additional capabilities include cable routing, bundling, labeling, kitting, and the manufacture of custom test harnesses for validation and production support. Every assembly undergoes 100% continuity and hi-pot testing on a Cirris 4250 tester, with results traceable to each production run.

Complete Cable serves the automotive, appliance manufacturing, industrial equipment, and electromechanical systems sectors, providing OEM assemblies built to customer specifications. The company supports engineering and production teams with rapid prototype builds and validation test support.

The company emphasizes responsive quoting—typically within 48 business hours—expedited prototype options, and direct access to ownership for fast decisions. A small, agile team manages process-controlled assembly with documented inspection, aiming to reduce rework and maintain dependable lead times based on material availability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Build-to-print wire harness and cable assembly manufacturing", "Wire cutting, stripping, crimping, and harness assembly", "Multi-gauge wire processing (14\u201322 AWG, PVC and SRPVC insulation)", "Cable routing, bundling, labeling, and kitting", "Custom test harness assemblies for validation and production support", "Rapid prototype builds", "100% continuity testing (Cirris 4250)", "Hi-pot testing", "Process-controlled assembly with documented inspection and testing", "Organized order management from quote through shipment"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliance Manufacturing", "Industrial Equipment", "Electromechanical Systems"], "materials": ["PVC insulated wire", "SRPVC insulated wire", "14\u201322 AWG wire"], "equipment": ["Cirris 4250 continuity tester"], "volume": "Prototype, low-volume, and repeat production", "lead_time": "Expedited prototype builds available; lead times based on material availability and order requirements", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% continuity and hi-pot testing on every assembly (Cirris 4250)", "Quotes provided within 48 business hours", "Expedited prototype builds available", "Direct access to ownership for fast decisions", "Family-owned, small agile team focused on reliability"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned manufacturer in St. Joseph, Michigan -> /about", "Co-owners Rob Kasun and Jon Kasun -> /about", "Manufactures custom wire harnesses and cable assemblies for OEM applications -> /", "Build-to-print manufacturing from prototype through repeat production -> /capabilities", "Wire cutting, stripping, crimping, harness assembly -> /capabi